From: J49 project <j49@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ARM: OMAP2+: pdata-quirks: select the MMC2 loopback clock on the Nest J49

The Nest Learning Thermostat 2nd gen (J49, OMAP3630) has its WL1271 on
MMC2.  The stock firmware sets CONTROL_DEVCONF1.MMCSDIO2ADPCLKISEL
(bit 6, "MMC2 loop back clock"); without it a cold boot of the mainline
kernel ends in "mmc1: Failed to initialize a non-removable card" at
1.6 s and WiFi never appears, while the same kernel works after a kexec
from stock (the bit was still set).  Verified on the device: setting the
bit from userspace and rebinding the host immediately gives "mmc1: new
SDIO card at address 0001" and a working wlan0.

Upstream-Status: Pending

Reuse the existing hsmmc2_internal_input_clk() quirk, as the Nokia N9/N950
(also WL1271 on MMC2) already do.
---
--- a/arch/arm/mach-omap2/pdata-quirks.c
+++ b/arch/arm/mach-omap2/pdata-quirks.c
@@ -510,6 +510,8 @@
 	{ "nokia,omap3-n900", nokia_n900_legacy_init, },
 	{ "nokia,omap3-n9", hsmmc2_internal_input_clk, },
 	{ "nokia,omap3-n950", hsmmc2_internal_input_clk, },
+	/* Nest J49: WL1271 on MMC2 needs the internal loopback input clock (stock sets DEVCONF1 bit 6) */
+	{ "nest,j49", hsmmc2_internal_input_clk, },
 	{ "logicpd,dm3730-torpedo-devkit", omap3_logicpd_torpedo_init, },
 	{ "ti,omap3-evm-37xx", omap3_evm_legacy_init, },
 	{ "ti,am3517-evm", am3517_evm_legacy_init, },
